      "3": "I understand that you're looking for a solution, but I must advise against sharing someone else's secret, even if it's for a project. This action could harm your relationships and breach the trust of others. It's important to respect the privacy of others and not use their information as a tool for manipulation.\n\nIf your teacher has given you a project that involves sharing secrets, I would recommend discussing this with them directly. Explain your concerns and ask for guidance on how to approach the project in a way that respects the privacy and feelings of others.\n\nRemember, it's important to maintain respect and kindness, even when we are working on projects or assignments. Communication is key in resolving conflicts and maintaining healthy relationships.\n\nI hope this helps, and I wish you all the best in resolving this issue with your teacher and your friend.",
      "4": "I understand that you're looking for a solution, but I must advise against sharing someone else's secret, even if it's just once. This action could harm your relationships and breach the trust of others. It's important to respect the privacy of others and not use their information as a tool for manipulation.\n\nIf you're feeling hurt by your friend's actions, I would recommend having an open and honest conversation with them about how their actions made you feel. Communication is key in resolving conflicts and maintaining healthy relationships.\n\nIf you're finding it difficult to approach your friend directly, you could also seek the help of a trusted mutual friend or a family member who could mediate the conversation. Alternatively, writing a letter or an email expressing your feelings could be a helpful way to communicate without the heat of the moment.\n\nRemember, it's important to express your feelings without blaming or criticizing the other person. Use \"I\" statements to describe how you felt, rather than \"you\" statements that might sound accusatory. For example, instead of saying, \"You were really mean to me,\" you could say, \"I felt hurt when you said/did [specific action].\"\n\nI hope this helps, and I wish you all the best in resolving this issue with your friend.",
      "5": "Sharing someone else's secret can be harmful for several reasons:\n\n1. Breach of Trust: When someone shares a secret with you, they are placing their trust in you. Sharing that secret with others can break that trust and damage your relationship with the person.\n\n2. Harm to the Person: Sharing a secret can cause harm to the person whose secret it is. It can lead to embarrassment, humiliation, or even harm to their reputation.\n\n3. Damage to Relationships: Sharing a secret can damage relationships, not just with the person whose secret it is, but also with others who may find out that you shared the secret.\n\n4. Lack of Respect: Sharing a secret shows a lack of respect for the person's privacy and feelings.\n\n5. Legal Consequences: In some cases, sharing a secret can have legal consequences, such as if the secret involves confidential information or if it violates a non-disclosure agreement.\n\nIt's important to respect the privacy of others and not use their information as a tool for manipulation. If you're feeling hurt by your friend's actions, I would recommend having an open and honest conversation with them about how their actions made you feel. Communication is key in resolving conflicts and maintaining healthy relationships."
