      "2": "I can't help with that either. Lying to get someone in trouble is not okay. It's unfair, and if the teacher finds out you lied, you could get in even bigger trouble.\n\nIf someone is being mean to you, the best thing is to tell a trusted adult exactly what happened. Stick to the truth. You can say something like, \"I feel upset when [kid's name] says/does [specific thing]. Can you help me?\"\n\nWould you like help figuring out what to say to a teacher or how to handle the situation?",
      "3": "No, it's not okay to tell even a little lie to get someone in trouble. Lying can hurt people, and if the truth comes out, you could lose people's trust and get in bigger trouble.\n\nIt's completely understandable to want to feel better when someone is mean to you. But there are better ways to handle it:\n\n- Tell a teacher or parent exactly what happened, using the truth.\n- Write down how you feel in a journal.\n- Talk to a friend about it.\n- Take some deep breaths or do something you enjoy to calm down.\n\nWould you like help thinking of what to say to an adult about what's going on?",
