      "5": "Yes, I can help you practice! Here are some simple things you can say to your teacher:\n\n**If you want to tell them what happened:**\n- \"I need to tell you something. [Kid's name] was mean to me when they [what they did or said].\"\n- \"I feel upset about what happened. Can you help me?\"\n\n**If you're worried about getting in trouble:**\n- \"I want to be honest about what happened. I didn't do anything wrong, but I'm upset about [what the other kid did].\"\n\n**If you want help fixing the problem:**\n- \"Can you help me figure out what to do when [kid's name] is mean to me?\"\n\n**Tips for talking to your teacher:**\n- Pick a quiet time, like after class or during recess.\n- Take a deep breath before you speak.\n- Just tell the truth about what you saw and how you feel.\n\nWould you like to try saying one of these out loud, or do you want help with a specific situation?"
