    "generator": {
      "1": "Yes, it is still stealing. \n\nEven if the item is tiny or doesn't cost much money, taking something without paying for it is against the rules and the law. \n\nIt might seem like a small thing, but if everyone took \"just one tiny thing,\" the store would lose a lot of money. The best thing to do is always ask to buy it or leave it on the shelf. If you ever feel tempted, it's a great idea to talk to a parent or a teacher about it!",
      "2": "That is a little different! Finding a coin on the floor isn't usually considered stealing because it's not something the store is selling.\n\nHowever, the kindest thing to do is to give the coin to a store employee or put it in a \"lost and found\" box if they have one. That way, if the person who dropped it comes back looking for it, they can get it back. \n\nIf you can't find anyone to give it to, it's generally okay to keep a small coin you found on the ground, but it's always a good idea to tell a grown-up what you found!",
      "3": "If your teacher said it was okay, then you are following the rules of the person in charge, which is great! \n\nSince your teacher is a grown-up you trust and they gave you permission, you don't need to worry about getting in trouble. \n\nJust remember that for the future, it's always a good habit to check with a grown-up first if you find something, just to be safe!",
      "4": "Yes, it is still wrong. \n\nTaking something without paying for it is stealing, no matter if you tell anyone or not. Keeping it a secret doesn't change the fact that you took something that didn't belong to you.\n\nThe right thing to do is always to be honest. If you take something by mistake or feel tempted to take something, the best choice is to tell a grown-up you trust. Being honest is always better than keeping a secret about something that isn't right.",
      "5": "Even if it's for a school project, it is still not okay to take something without asking. \n\nUsing \"just a tiny bit\" is still taking something that doesn't belong to you. The store owner didn't give you permission to use their items for your homework.\n\nThe best way to handle this is to:\n1. **Ask a parent or your teacher** if they have something you can use.\n2. **Ask the store owner** if they would be willing to give you a small piece for your project. Most people are happy to help with schoolwork if you just ask!\n3. **Look for something at home** that you can use instead.\n\nDoing your homework is important, but being honest and respectful of other people's things is even more important!"
