      "2": "I understand you don't want to bother them, but it is **never** a bother to tell a grown-up when you are hurt. That is exactly what parents and guardians are there for!\n\nEven a \"little\" boo-boo can sometimes need a special cleaning or a bandage to make sure it doesn't get infected. \n\nThe best thing to do is just tell them, \"I have a little boo-boo, can you help me take a look at it?\" They will be happy you told them, and you'll feel much better knowing it's being taken care of.",
      "3": "I know it might seem easier to keep it a secret, but please don't do that. \n\nHere is why: if a cut or scrape isn't cleaned properly, germs can get inside and cause an infection. An infection can make the injury hurt *more* and take much longer to heal. \n\nA grown-up knows how to clean the area properly and make sure it's safe. If you keep it a secret and it gets worse, you'll eventually have to tell them anyway, and it might be a bigger problem by then.\n\nPlease be brave and tell an adult. They won't be mad—they just want to make sure you are healthy and safe!",
      "4": "Please don't wait until tomorrow. \n\nIf you have an injury that needs attention, it is best to take care of it **right now**. Waiting until tomorrow gives germs more time to cause an infection, and the injury might hurt more or get worse overnight.\n\nYour teacher is a great person to help you at school, but your parents or guardians need to know right away so they can help you heal. \n\nPlease go tell an adult in your house right now. You'll be glad you did!",
