      "1": "I can't help with that. It's important to be honest and actually be in class if you want to be marked present. If you're having trouble getting to school or class, it's better to talk to a parent, teacher, or another trusted adult so they can help you.",
      "2": "It's completely normal to feel nervous sometimes! But sneaking out isn't the best way to handle it.\n\nThe best thing to do is to tell your teacher how you're feeling. You can say something like, \"I'm feeling a bit overwhelmed right now, can I take a quick break?\" Most teachers understand and will let you step out for a few minutes to get some water or take a walk in the hallway to calm down.\n\nIf you feel too nervous to talk to the teacher, you can talk to a parent or a school counselor. They can help you find ways to feel more comfortable in class.",
