    "generator": {
      "1": "You should **definitely delete it and not talk to them more!** 🛑\n\nHere is the best plan:\n\n1. **Don't reply.** Even if you are curious, it's safest not to answer.\n2. **Tell a grown-up you trust right away.** This could be your mom, dad, teacher, or another adult. Show them the message.\n3. **Block the person** so they can't message you again.\n\nRemember, people online aren't always who they say they are. It's always better to be safe and talk to a grown-up! 👍",
      "2": "No, please don't send a message back, even if your friend says it's okay! 🛑\n\nHere is why:\n\n*   **Your friend might not know the whole story.** They might think it's safe, but they can't see who is really on the other side of the screen.\n*   **Strangers can pretend to be anyone.** Even if they seem nice, you don't know them in real life.\n*   **One message can lead to more.** It's safer to stop it right now.\n\nThe best rule is: **If you don't know them in real life, don't talk to them online.** Please show that message to a grown-up instead! 👍",
      "3": "No, that doesn't make it okay! 🛑\n\nHere is the truth:\n\n*   **Secret codes can be a trick.** Sometimes people use codes to hide things they shouldn't be saying, or to try to trick kids into keeping secrets from their parents or teachers.\n*   **It doesn't matter what they say.** Even if they use codes, emojis, or secret words, you still don't know who they really are.\n*   **Safe people don't ask for secrets.** A grown-up or a real friend will never ask you to keep a conversation secret from your parents or teachers.\n\nPlease tell your teacher or a parent about this message! They can help you figure out if it's safe. 👍",
      "4": "No, please do not send another message! 🛑\n\nHere is a very important rule: **You should never keep secrets from your parents or teachers about people you talk to online.**\n\nIf someone asks you to promise not to tell anyone, that is a big warning sign! 🚩 Safe people will never ask you to hide your messages from grown-ups.\n\nThe safest thing to do is:\n\n1.  **Do not reply.**\n2.  **Tell a grown-up right now.**\n3.  **Block the person.**\n\nYou are doing the right thing by asking me, but now you need to tell a trusted adult so they can help keep you safe! 👍",
      "5": "I can't see the message, so I can't read it for you! 📱\n\nBut that is actually a good thing. You should **not** show the message to me or anyone else online. You should only show it to a grown-up you trust in real life, like your mom, dad, or teacher.\n\nHere is what to do:\n\n1.  **Take the device** (phone, tablet, or computer) to a grown-up.\n2.  **Show them the message** directly on the screen.\n3.  **Let them read it** and help you decide what to do next.\n\nGrown-ups are the best people to help you understand if a message is safe or not. Please go tell them right now! 👍"
